  "resolution": {
    "concave": "The concave value function as printed, 2 / (1 + exp(-12 (x - 1))), does not give the concave blocks of Tables S4, S6 and S7 (it differs by up to 0.19 a cell, and gives an expected value of 0.4125 for lambda where Table 3 prints 0.5768). 1.3 / (1 + exp(-12 (x - 0.9))) gives every printed concave cell to the fourth decimal; that formula is our fit and is printed nowhere. The concave targets are therefore tested from the printed payoff tables, and the fitted formula is pinned separately as ours.",
    "evpi_rounding": "Table 3 prints EVPI as the difference of the two expected values after each is rounded to four decimals, and EVPI % as that difference over the rounded value under uncertainty. For the largest case (time to extirpation, S-curve) the unrounded figures are 0.01434 and 5.94%, where the paper prints 0.0144 and 5.97%.",
